# Phase-4 replay archive — trade domain under link faults: three interactions
# sent back-to-back while both directions carry a 200 ms delay. The reliable
# channels preserve send order, so the guest must receive EXACTLY the host's
# three authoritative overwrites in order, and the last one must equal the
# host's final state. The trade actions' SimTrace result is "Sent" here — the
# report is in flight at the action step; the convergence assertion is the
# verdict.
#
# Fossil of: TradeSimulationTests.Interaction_UnderLinkDelay_StillConverges
# Mechanism: FakeNetwork delay faults + TradeChannel reliable FIFO

@0 fault g1 host delay=200
@0 fault host g1 delay=200
@0 trade g1 meet
@0 trade g1 haggle
@0 trade g1 move
@600 expect trade_received g1 3 within 1000
@600 expect trade_converged g1
